    "smallest_supported_mechanism": "The Float64-assembled canonical Hessian loses the low-eigenvalue information before the eigensolver: its scaled matrix differs from the high-precision matrix built from the same frozen inputs by about 3.98e-17 in relative infinity norm, while the leading Hessian condition number is about 3.48e73. A high-precision eigensolve of the promoted Float64 matrix still yields low-mode masses near 13.238, 13.843, and 13.999 with signs (+,+,-), rather than the frozen-input high-precision values near -12.919, -4.598, and -1.963 with all-positive signs. The Float64 solver changes these already damaged modes further to the P0 Float64 observations. Thus Float64 assembly precision is sufficient to explain loss of low modes in this fixture; solver sensitivity contributes to the final observed values.",
